{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788305667,"nonce":"Avss4G9dJQEXw7gpv4vhs9g6Vc0=","title":"accept/fc287ba-until-state.py --dry-run crashes in phase 3: the plan for three of its five phases has never been printable","message":"`accept/fc287ba-until-state.py --dry-run` crashes in phase 3 with a `TypeError`, so the plan for phases 3-5 has never been printable and the `--dry-run` mode cannot be used to review that suite.\n\n```\n    target = (hour + 1) % 24\n              ~~~~~^~~\nTypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for +: 'NoneType' and 'int'\n```\n\nFound on 2026-09-01 while working `280fb78` (the suite was on the read list because `until:{letter}` was thought to be at risk there). **Pre-existing and not caused by that branch** — reproduced against `git show main:accept/fc287ba-until-state.py` at `a2bf74f`, byte-identical to the file on main.\n\n## Cause\n\nUnder `--dry-run`, `send()` returns `{\"ok\": True, \"op\": op, \"data\": {}, \"_dry\": True}` — an empty `data` — so every helper that digs a value out of a live envelope returns `None`. Phase 3 reads the clock and then does arithmetic on it. `accept/722c951-advance-halt.py` hit the same class of thing and guards it with `ARGS.dry_run or isinstance(t, int)` in a `precondition()`; this suite does not.\n\nThe other suites in `accept/` print their plan end to end (`280fb78` 107 checks, `722c951` 92), so this one is the outlier rather than the norm.\n\n## Why it matters more than a crashing flag\n\n`--dry-run` is how a suite is reviewed WITHOUT a bench, and the orchestrator's normal workflow is to review a suite while the bench is busy. A suite whose plan cannot be printed past phase 2 gets reviewed by reading the source instead, which is exactly the check `--dry-run` exists to replace.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- `./accept/fc287ba-until-state.py --dry-run` exits 0 and prints the planned checks for every phase, 1 through 5.\n- The fix is a dry-run guard on the values read from the game, not a `try/except` around the arithmetic: a `None` that flows into a check should surface as a printed expectation, never be swallowed.\n- Any other value phases 3-5 dig out of a live envelope and then compute with is guarded the same way — grep the file for arithmetic on a `dig()` result, do not fix only the one line in the traceback.\n- `./accept/fc287ba-until-state.py --selftest` — or, if this suite has no selftest, `--dry-run` — is added to whatever the round runs offline, so the mode cannot silently rot again.","files":null}]}